__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
.venv/
venv/
.env
# Any .env variant - NOT just ".env". A `cp .env .env.bak-151721`
# safety copy made before editing was matched by none of these rules,
# got swept up by `git add -A`, and was pushed to GitHub with every
# secret in it (2026-09-24 - the bot token was stolen and used within
# hours). The negation keeps the committed template tracked.
.env.*
!.env.dist

# Everything the bot writes lives under data/ (see paths.py):
#   data/cache/  refetchable caches and derived indexes (codex.sqlite3,
#                textindex, the Discord harvest + image transcriptions, ...)
#   data/state/  live state: reminders, amities, nicknames, usage stats,
#                announce chats, browser logins - back these up
# data/qa_crawl/ is deliberately COMMITTED: the raw r/OrnaRPG crawl (800
# threads) took an hour of rate-limited fetching to build, and keeping it lets
# scrapers/orna_scrape_qa.py resume from any checkout.
data/cache/
data/state/
